  "analysis": "Starting fresh. I need to build POV-Ray 2.2, which is a 1993-era program. First I need to survey the environment: OS type, available compilers, and network access to find the old source archives.",
  "plan": "Check /etc/os-release, list /app, and see what tools (gcc, make, tar) are available. Then probe the network for download options.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /etc/os-release; echo ---; ls -la /app /app/deps 2>&1 | head -50\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which gcc make tar wget curl bzip2 gzip; gcc --version 2>&1 | head -2\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes " : "timeout 8 bash -c 'echo > /dev/tcp/sourceforge.net/80' 2>&1 && echo SF_OK || echo SF_FAIL\n",
      "duration": 10.0
    }
  ]
}

